WEBVTT


00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.020
I just dropped Claude dashboards

00:00:02.021 --> 00:00:04.101
and you don't want to miss out on this.

00:00:04.102 --> 00:00:06.961
So here's how to set it up in three simple steps.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.820
Step 1, you're gonna connect your data.

00:00:08.821 --> 00:00:10.501
You can choose your tool of choice,

00:00:10.502 --> 00:00:12.221
whether it's Salesforce, Snowflake,

00:00:12.222 --> 00:00:14.221
or whatever you're using. Step 2,

00:00:14.222 --> 00:00:16.461
ask a question in plain English,

00:00:16.462 --> 00:00:20.001
something like, how did this week's signups compared to last month's?

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.780
Claude writes the code and builds the whole dashboard for you,

00:00:23.781 --> 00:00:26.501
but with a catch. And this is my favourite part,

00:00:26.502 --> 00:00:29.581
step 3. It stays live as your data changes,

00:00:29.582 --> 00:00:31.241
your dashboard updates.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.700
You no longer need to prompt a file or an artifact.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.021
And if you don't trust a number,

00:00:36.022 --> 00:00:39.781
you can click on it and Claude shows you exactly how it worked it out.

00:00:39.782 --> 00:00:41.061
So it's in beta right now,

00:00:41.062 --> 00:00:43.721
but it's getting rolled out gradually to some accounts.
